      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DON HUNTER (1) makes his first appearance since a midfield finish in July's Protostar in Brisbane but was readied with an easy trial win. Unbeaten in three tries at this circuit and distance including a Sapling Stakes and the APG Final. The ace draw gives him every chance for a winning return. OH ITS ON (7) is a progressive colt who has won three of four starts since joining Jason Grimson for this campaign. Led from this barrier for an easy Tatlow Stakes win two back at this circuit and distance before cruising home at Bathurst. Danger with the fitness edge. TUAPEKA GOLD (6) won his first three starts before copping back row draws in both rounds of the Nutrien series. Hasn't raced since May but was readied with two nice trials. ROGUE BANDIT (2) raced parked in a resuming fourth to a top filly. Draws lower and should strip fitter so may improve.",
